<header><p class="st-kicker">protectorate · West Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Kamerun</h1><p class="st-meta">1884 CE – 1916 CE · capital Buea</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The German colony in Central Africa, founded through treaties with the Duala in 1884, which expanded deep into the interior before Allied forces conquered it in 1916.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>On 12 July 1884 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duala-people">Duala</a> kings Bell and Akwa signed a treaty with German agents, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gustav-nachtigal">Gustav Nachtigal</a> raised the German flag at the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duala-kingdoms">Duala kingdoms</a> days later. From the coast German forces pushed inland over the next twenty years, defeating resistance from peoples such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulu-people">Bulu</a> and from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fula">Fulbe</a> lamidates like <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lamidate-of-ngaoundere">Ngaoundere</a>, until the colony reached <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-chad">Lake Chad</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>German rule depended on concession companies and plantations on the slopes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mount-cameroon">Mount Cameroon</a>, worked by forced and recruited labour; the governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesko-von-puttkamer">Jesko von Puttkamer</a> (1895-1907) was notorious for abuses. The seat of government moved between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duala-people">Duala</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buea">Buea</a>, on the cooler slopes of Mount <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cameroon">Cameroon</a>. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agadir-crisis">Agadir crisis</a> of 1911 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> ceded large territories, called <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neukamerun">Neukamerun</a>, from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-equatorial-africa">French Equatorial Africa</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1914 the Germans hanged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rudolf-duala-manga-bell">Rudolf Duala Manga Bell</a> for resisting land expropriation. British and French forces conquered Kamerun in 1914-1916, and it was divided into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-cameroon">French Cameroon</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/british-cameroons">British Cameroons</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kamerun.jpg" alt="Kamerun" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Original: Imperial Colonial Office of the German Empire Vector: David Liuzzo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Reichskolonialflagge.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1884 CE – 1916 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>protectorate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Buea</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Julius von Soden, Jesko von Puttkamer, Theodor Seitz</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Traditional religion, Christianity, Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German, Duala, Fulfulde</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/cameroon">Cameroon</a>, <a href="/countries/nigeria">Nigeria</a>, <a href="/countries/chad">Chad</a>, <a href="/countries/central-african-republic">Central African Republic</a>, <a href="/countries/gabon">Gabon</a>, <a href="/countries/republic-of-the-congo">Republic of the Congo</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>German Kamerun, German Cameroon, Schutzgebiet Kamerun</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1900&amp;focus=kamerun" aria-label="Kamerun on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4936 2022 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kamerun lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5256 2278L5256 2278M5256 2278L5345 2090M5256 2278L5382 1985M5256 2278L5389 2022M5256 2278L5303 2220M5256 2278L5269 2282M5256 2278L5300 622M5256 2278L4997 651M5256 2278L5320 2289M5256 2278L5295 2202M5256 2278L5280 2206M5256 2278L5278 2214"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5256 2278h0M5345 2090h0M5382 1985h0M5389 2022h0M5303 2220h0M5269 2282h0M5300 622h0M4997 651h0M5320 2289h0M5295 2202h0M5280 2206h0M5278 2214h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5256 2278h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5256 2278h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Buea. <a href="/atlas?year=1900&amp;focus=kamerun">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

